  "course_description": "Seminar on various anthropological topics. Satisfies general education Freshman Seminar.",
  "course_notes": "(Same as AAS 190 1 and AFS 190 1) (Freshmen Seminar - Limited to First Year Students Only) (This course will consider the African continent within a global perspective. African societies have always played an important role in global transformations. From the era of the slave trade, through colonialism, and into the present, Africa has shaped and has been shaped by global forces. This course will explore this history as well as contemporary examples of Africa's engagement with the world. We will consider economic projects, political movements, and artistic forms that demonstrate this engagement. Course materials will include academic books, articles, and films.)",
